@page "/spaces/{SpaceId:guid}/projects/{ProjectId:guid}"

@*
    A PROJECT'S BOARD - the product's primary surface (story 2.2). FR-19, FR-28; UX-DR8, UX-DR26, UX-DR27,
    UX-DR31, UX-DR33, UX-DR35.

    ARRIVES LIKE EVERY SPACE-SCOPED PAGE, through SpaceArrival: an unlisted Space is refused with no
    request, the active Space is asked first, nothing of the Board renders before the server has answered,
    every 404 - the Space's or the Project's - renders the one refusal surface, and a 401 is
    YelloApiHandler's. Re-navigating to the same Board keeps it, and an open Task creation with its text,
    while the Role is re-read (AC14).

    THE ADDRESS HOLDS IDS ONLY, and no Project or Task name reaches the document's title, which stays the product's name
    (UX-DR33). The Space leads the path, so the purge hook reads it as it reads Space home's.

    THE BOARD ITSELF is BoardView's, keyed on (Space, Project) so another Project starts a new Board
    rather than reusing this one's columns.
*@

<SpaceArrival SpaceId="@SpaceId" Context="arrival">
    <BoardView @key="(SpaceId, ProjectId)"
               SpaceId="@SpaceId"
               ProjectId="@ProjectId"
               RoleCode="@arrival.Current.Role"
               OnRefused="arrival.Refuse" />
</SpaceArrival>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The Space this route names.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Guid SpaceId { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The Project whose Board this is.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Guid ProjectId { get; set; }
}
